&lt;div class="col-label"&gt;What it claims&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The Machine&lt;br&gt;Can See&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class="col-body"&gt;Context.&nbsp; Space.&nbsp; Physical reality.&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="col-label accent"&gt;What it does&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3 class="accent"&gt;Word-Based&lt;br&gt;Reasoning&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class="col-body"&gt;Pixels → Tokens → Expected output.&lt;/div&gt;



On the left: what the marketing says. The machine can see. Context. Space. Physical reality.
On the right: what the architecture does. Converts pixels to tokens. Reasons about the tokens as language. Outputs what it was trained to expect.
One is perception. The other is a very sophisticated performance of it.
