The LanguageBottleneck



&lt;div class="tl-dot burst"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="tl-label"&gt;Pixels&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="tl-desc"&gt;Visual input enters the system as raw data points.&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;div class="tl-dot"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="tl-label"&gt;Tokens&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="tl-desc"&gt;Converted to language before any high-level reasoning occurs.&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;div class="tl-dot burst"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="tl-label accent"&gt;Expected World&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="tl-desc"&gt;The system describes a statistical probability, not reality.&lt;/div&gt;



[Gesture across the diagram — one pass, no elaboration.]
At no point in that pipeline is there genuine visual reasoning.
At every point, there is a very convincing Wally.
